        file-1kwcbevmrazyyhvluhvhxy
        . This is a hypothesis that should be labeled as such.

        Entropy “no longer volumetric” beyond $T_c$: This claim – that above a certain density/temperature, entropy must go to the surface – is speculative. It’s one possible way to resolve the dilemma, but not a proven one. Established physics would say when you reach extreme compactness, you form a black hole and then the description of entropy in the interior is inaccessible; the author is adding the idea of a phase transition at the horizon formation. This is a conjectural mechanism. It should be noted as an assumption of the model. The paper provides plausibility (via the volume vs entropy calc), but no rigorous proof that nature indeed enforces this threshold. For example, one could ask: does every object at $1.4\times10^{29}$ K necessarily become a black hole? We don’t actually know – we’ve never tested physics anywhere near that regime. So while it’s reasonable to suspect new physics kicks in, the exact threshold is not known. This is the author’s speculative interpretation of how holography might come about in a collapse.

        “Quantum stabilization” and 2D interior: The notion that the black hole interior becomes a stable, two-dimensional quantum system​
        file-1kwcbevmrazyyhvluhvhxy
